{%- comment -%}
  gs-header: the site header (DESIGN.md §6.1). Draft reference: untested until the theme is pulled.

  Works without JavaScript. The Menu drawer and every dropdown are <details> elements, so all
  links are reachable even if assets/gs-nav.js fails to load. The script adds Escape, closing on
  an outside click, and (desktop) closing when focus leaves a dropdown.

  The main menu renders twice: in the drawer (below 1200px) and in the bar (1200px and up).
  CSS shows only one, so assistive tech only ever finds one "Main" navigation. In each, the
  markup order matches what's on screen: the bar's utility row sits above the nav, so it comes
  first; in the drawer the utility links follow the nav.

  Params
    menu          main menu linklist, e.g. linklists[section.settings.menu]
    utility_menu  small linklist: Contact, Newsletter, Search. The cart link is added here.

  Example (sections/gs-header.liquid)
    {%- render 'gs-header', menu: linklists[section.settings.menu], utility_menu: linklists[section.settings.utility_menu] -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- capture utility -%}
  <ul class="gs-utility">
    {%- for link in utility_menu.links -%}
      {%- capture r -%}{%- render 'gs-url', link: link -%}{%- endcapture -%}
      {%- assign r = r | strip | split: '|' -%}
      <li><a href="{{ r[0] }}"{% if link.current %} aria-current="page"{% endif %}>{{ link.title | strip | escape }}</a></li>
    {%- endfor -%}
    <li><a href="{{ routes.cart_url }}">Cart ({{ cart.item_count }})</a></li>
  </ul>
{%- endcapture -%}
<header class="gs-header" data-gs-header>
  <a class="gs-header__logo" href="{{ routes.root_url }}" aria-label="Gordon Smith Gallery, home">
    {%- render 'gs-logo', name: 'gallery-simple-stacked-colour-box', label: 'decorative' -%}
  </a>

  <details class="gs-drawer">
    <summary class="gs-header__menu-toggle">Menu</summary>
    <div class="gs-drawer__panel">
      <nav aria-label="Main">
        {%- render 'gs-nav', menu: menu, variant: 'drawer' -%}
      </nav>
      {{ utility }}
    </div>
  </details>

  <div class="gs-header__bar">
    {{ utility }}
    <nav aria-label="Main">
      {%- render 'gs-nav', menu: menu, variant: 'bar' -%}
    </nav>
  </div>
</header>
